    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Grew up amid the Belgian Congo occupation under King Leopold; fell under the sway of a charismatic local conqueror consumed by dark passion, and fled in panic after his death. Forcibly Embraced by Elias Bruylant, a 200-year-old @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.phgt6OMwTAoAaKfR]{Lasombra} who had built a haven on the Congo's Sangha tributary and marked her as promising. Traveled to Europe after her sire deemed her ready, and was dazzled by its empires and philosophies; joined the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat}'s cause. Cardinal Monçada tried to convert her to his theology for years without success — she considered his God to be her Devil. Took the name &quot;Conrad&quot; in the 1920s after Joseph Conrad, whose writing about Congo horrors spoke to her. Came to the Americas during the Depression and has since stirred up trouble in Black communities across the hemisphere, curious whether persecution breeds more vampires like herself; she instructs new recruits in @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.phgt6OMwTAoAaKfR]{Lasombra} history and powers between personal ventures.</p><p><strong>Sire:</strong> Elias Bruylant.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Conrad is a sharp, watchful survivor who tests people's convictions the way the Congo tested hers. She is fascinated, not sentimental, about suffering and its capacity to create monsters like herself.</p><p><strong>Stat Block (as printed):</strong><br><strong>Physical:</strong> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br><strong>Social:</strong> Charisma 3, Manipulation 4, Appearance 2<br><strong>Mental:</strong> Perception 4, Intelligence 4, Wits 3<br><strong>Disciplines:</strong> Dominate 2, Obfuscate 3, Obtenebration 5, Potence 1<br><strong>Virtues:</strong> Conviction 3, Self-Control 3, Courage 5<br><strong>Morality:</strong> @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.paths-of-enlightenment.JournalEntry.n1ghtP4thOfN1ght]{Path of Night} (Cold Path) 6<br><strong>Willpower:</strong> 7</p>",
    "notes": "Convert Disciplines to owned power Items: Dominate 2, Obfuscate 3, Obtenebration 5, Potence 1 (dot ratings preserved as printed; select individual powers up to those ratings at Storyteller discretion).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
